  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "NVIDIA's NVFP4 (ModelOpt) quantization of Google Gemma 4 26B-A4B IT on one Spark with vLLM v0.25.1 plus upstream's patched gemma4.py (ModelOpt lm_head tying): 262144-token context, fp8 KV cache, 18 concurrent sequences, MTP speculative decoding (1 token) with Google's gemma-4-26B-A4B-it-assistant, one image per prompt, thinking on by default, Gemma 4 reasoning and tool-call parsers. Basis: MiaAI-Lab's 18-concurrency start.sh (no licence file upstream; gemma4.py keeps vLLM's Apache-2.0 header). Upstream runs the mutable vllm-openai:nightly of July 2026; this recipe pins v0.25.1, whose gemma4.py differs from the patch by 13 lines. Model and assistant are under Google's Gemma terms (recorded as information). Upstream throughput figures (about 282 tok/s at 18 sessions) are its claims; Vonk physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
